package CanvasNet {
    part def ScaleResolver {
        doc /* The internal static ScaleResolver with the ResolvedScales, ResolvedScale, and RangeEnd types: it infers, for each encoding channel of a single view, the scale Vega-Lite would build, as a description that is independent of the size of the data rectangle until ResolvedScale.CreateModel is given it. Rules (ported from Vega-Lite and Vega with attribution): quantitative positions are linear and discrete positions are band scales for rect, bar, image, rule, and tick marks and point scales otherwise;         color, fill, and stroke fields are ordinal (the named range category or ordinal of config.range, the scale's range or scheme) and a quantitative color is a sequential scale (diverging with a middle value) over the ramp, heatmap, or diverging range, a named scheme or a list of colors interpolated in the color space that interpolate names; quantize, quantile, and threshold scales classify (five scheme colors by default, quantileCount and quantizeCount 4 for the spread numbers of a size, thresholds plus one); shape, strokeDash, strokeWidth, fillOpacity, strokeOpacity, and angle have scales for the marks that use them (Vega-Lite's supportMark) with the symbol list, five dash patterns, and default numeric ranges; rangeMin and rangeMax replace the entries of a default range; an unknown scheme name or named range is a VegaLiteSpecException as in Vega; size and opacity use the default ranges of the mark; the linear domain is the extent of the valid values with the zero rule, domainMin, domainMax, and domainMid, an explicit domain (all entries kept, so a domain and range of more than two entries map piecewise; zero, padding, and nice change only the end entries), nice, and pixel padding applied in Vega's order; a band or point scale uses the first two entries of its range; a discrete domain is sorted ascending by default (sort may be ascending, descending, null, an array, an encoding sort such as "-y" or an object with an encoding channel and an order, or an object with any orderable aggregate op - count, valid, missing, distinct, sum, product, mean, average, median, q1, q3, min, max, the variances and deviations, stderr, and the interval ends - an optional field, and an optional order, which orders the categories by that aggregate over the rows of the raw table, stably, a category without a valid number first, via IsSupportedFieldSort and the MeasureCell accumulators of the AggregateTransforms unit); Phase 6 makes the resolver plan driven (the partial files ScaleResolver.Plan.cs and ScaleResolver.Sort.cs): it reads the field that the EncodingPlan names for each channel (the bin start, the aggregate measure, or the end of a stack), builds the domain of a stacked channel from the start and end values (0 to 1 for a normalized stack), of a range channel from the union of a field and its secondary field, of a binned channel from the start of the first and the end of the last bin without zero or nice, of a pre-binned channel from the union of its start and end, and of a scale with the domain "unaggregated" from the extent of the raw field, and gives a discrete bin the labels of its ranges ordered by bin start; paddings follow the mark and the scale configuration; a step-driven discrete scale reports the extent the view needs; InferOrient gives the horizontal or vertical orientation of bar, tick, and rule marks. An invalid scale domain, range, or scheme is a VegaLiteSpecException with the pointer, a discrete domain, a range, or a scheme count beyond MaxScaleDomainSize is a VegaLiteRenderException, the values of a quantile scale are counted against the cell limit and charged to the evaluation-step budget, and cancellation is polled while the data is scanned and sorted. */
                comment sourceRef /* Source: src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/Scales/ScaleResolver.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/Scales/ScaleResolver.Plan.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/Scales/ScaleResolver.Sort.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/Scales/ScaleResolver.Color.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/Scales/ScaleResolver.Range.cs */
                comment testRef /* Test: test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/Scales/ScaleResolverTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/Scales/ScaleResolverPlanTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/Scales/ScaleResolverColorTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/Transforms/RowTransformsTests.cs (the sort-by-field tests) */
        comment designRef /* Design: docs/design/canvas-net-vega-lite/scales/scale-resolver.md */
        comment verificationRef /* Verification: docs/verification/canvas-net-vega-lite/scales/scale-resolver.md */
        comment reqRef /* Requirements: docs/reqstream/canvas-net-vega-lite/scales/scale-resolver.yaml */
    }
}
